  "prompt": "Is interest on a Philippine peso savings account subject to final withholding tax?",
  "runtimeCommit": "d71b913ddf39726234dd02d858fac3e5275e865b",
  "answer": "### Issue Presented\nYes, interest on a Philippine peso savings account is subject to final withholding tax at the rate of 20%. This is specified in Revenue Regulations No. 2-98, which implements provisions of the National Internal Revenue Code regarding income payments subject to final withholding tax.\n\n### Legal Interpretation\n\nThe withholding obligation arises when a withholding agent makes payment to a resident income payee for a service subject to withholding under applicable revenue regulations.\n\n### Practical Application\n\nThe payor must withhold the applicable rate, remit to the BIR, and issue BIR Form 2307 (certificate of creditable withholding tax) to the payee.",
